            text: "<div class=\"faq\"><b>This doesn't look like what my lab sends.</b><p>That is intentional. Features are built directly into the 3D-printed device for consistent, precise results. The Order Specs card shows exactly what was built into the device.</p></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Where is the Poron for my offloads?</b><p>Hike prints a soft Poron-like interface rather than creating a relief and adding Poron. The printed interface keeps its material properties over time \u2014 Poron degrades with repeated wear.</p></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Why is the wedge the same color as the base?</b><p>Extrinsic wedges are printed from the same material as the base as one continuous piece. There is no seam or second material.</p></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>I cannot see the met pad you built in.</b><p>Some modifications are printed directly into the base and covered by the top cover, so they are not visible from the outside. You can feel them through the top cover. The Order Specs card identifies exactly what was built in.</p></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Can you match a traditional polypropylene device?</b><p>The printing process replicates the functional properties of polypropylene, providing comparable firm control.</p></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Can I get it thinner or \u00be-length?</b><p>Yes. Hike offers standard thickness, a thinning taper, and \u00be-length options. For \u00be-length, the base is 0.8 mm with a full-length top cover.</p></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Can I adjust it in the clinic?</b><p>You should not need to \u2014 free remakes are available if something is not right. If an adjustment is necessary, diabetic EVA can be adjusted up to about 2 mm and cork-mimic can be adjusted slightly deeper. Never use a heat gun or place the device in an oven.</p></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>How fast will I get it?</b><p>Devices are manufactured and shipped within 5 business days.</p></div>",
